-806b-703ca14c80f8" :question/problem "Find the domain of $s(x)=\\sqrt[6]{2x-4}+1.$"] ["question-7823b972-423e-5466-806b-703ca14c80f8" :question/worked-solution "The domain of $y=\\sqrt[6]{x}$ is\n\n$$\nx\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nTo find the domain of $s(x)=\\sqrt[6]{2x-4}+1,$ we replace $x$ with $2x-4$ in the above inequality. This gives\n\n$$\n2x-4\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-4 & \\ge 0 \\\\ 2x & \\ge 4 \\\\ x & \\ge 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $y=s(x)$ is $x\\in [2,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=s(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/c3/c340fbe03170ab0dcd2ba0a7c7c32ed6712f96b0eaa944cde2dc40a232e3e32e.png)"] ["question-7823b972-423e-5466-806b-703ca14c80f8" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-c0e0985b-75bc-5d5f-8b91-eb1bc0518ee9" :answer-field/id #uuid "c0e0985b-75bc-5d5f-8b91-eb1bc0518ee9"] ["answer-6fc57805-d59e-554a-a8df-6378c378a54d" :answer/id #uuid "6fc57805-d59e-554a-a8df-6378c378a54d"] ["answer-6fc57805-d59e-554a-a8df-6378c378a54d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6fc57805-d59e-554a-a8df-6378c378a54d" :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2]"] ["answer-9f27a8ae-d48c-5273-8f21-4484bcd3f317" :answer/id #uuid "9f27a8ae-d48c-5273-8f21-4484bcd3f317"] ["answer-9f27a8ae-d48c-5273-8f21-4484bcd3f317" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9f27a8ae-d48c-5273-8f21-4484bcd3f317" :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,2]"] ["answer-83ea8867-972b-5a55-a003-4a969418a652" :answer/id #uuid "83ea8867-972b-5a55-a003-4a969418a652"] ["answer-83ea8867-972b-5a55-a003-4a969418a652" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-83ea8867-972b-5a55-a003-4a969418a652" :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["answer-d98d7ed4-b084-5a6e-a7ed-fc234b26f788" :answer/id #uuid "d98d7ed4-b084-5a6e-a7ed-fc234b26f788"] ["answer-d98d7ed4-b084-5a6e-a7ed-fc234b26f788" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d98d7ed4-b084-5a6e-a7ed-fc234b26f788" :answer/v